osed_at":"2025-03-19T09:35:35Z"},"comments":3,"created_at":"2024-12-27T15:01:46Z","updated_at":"2025-01-13T21:00:57Z","closed_at":"2025-01-13T19:28:55Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/100851","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100851","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100851.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100851.patch","merged_at":"2025-01-13T19:28:55Z"},"body":"Occasionally, when launching a game from the editor, I would observe a crash due to using a Metal object that had already been freed. This should be resolved by switching the `MTLCommandBuffer` to retaining references (which is was originally) and is the normal usage of the API. I will revisit using the optimised API in the future, when I can guarantee that references are always retained by the Metal rendering driver for the duration of the frame.\r\n\r\nI have also updated the availability API declarations to include `tvOS`, for any future work in this area, which should have no side effects to the editor or existing Apple platforms.\r\n\r\nFinally, the code which maps pixel formats had a number of `#ifdef`s for each platform, which was unnecessarily complex, and this has been condensed, so that it is shared across all platforms. As such, this will pave the way for future platform support, such as tvOS.","closed_by":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/gists{/gist_id}","starre